invariant: INV-16
file: srv_tcp_nonblocking.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_widemul
reason: ch_srv_record_init stops writing the session's answer into its record
  directions, so each record it seals or opens runs Poly1305 under 0, the
  decomposition, whatever the caller answered. The key exchange and the
  signature still follow the answer, so only a count of the record's
  copy notices: test/tcp_nonblocking_loop_widemul.h requires an end that answers
  CH_WIDEMUL_CONSTANT_TIME to call no file under its own names.

--- old
#ifdef CH_WIDEMUL_RUNTIME
    tlsi_record_widemul(&r->t);
#endif
--- new
